{
 "_": [
  "Every slayer helmet OSRS has, in a plain and an imbued form. tools/genslayerhelm.py turns this",
  "into their objs, the recolour interaction, and the unlock purchases.",
  "",
  "THESE ARE OSRS'S OWN MODELS, NOT RECOLOURS. The first version of this round tinted two colours",
  "on the plain helmet, which only ever touched the mask and the strap. OSRS's variants are",
  "separately authored meshes - the red one has different horns, the green one different spines,",
  "the hooded one is a hood - so each carries its own model set, imported by",
  "tools/models/importosrs.py from the obj id in osrs_obj and named obj_slayer_helm_<models>.",
  "The camera is the cache's own too: the plain helmet faces 1791 and every recolour 1773, and",
  "the hooded and oathplate ones are different again.",
  "",
  "geom IS THE ANCHOR. osrs_model is the cache model this colour was imported from, and geom is that",
  "model's vertex and face counts after conversion, recorded at import time. Without it, a colour",
  "pointed at the WRONG model set would be self-consistent - the config would say what the spec says",
  "and every check would agree - because the cache is not on the laptop to ask. Battery group 67",
  "measures the shipped .ob2 files against these numbers instead. They are all distinct except",
  "oathplate and radiant, which really are one mesh.",
  "",
  "recol IS ONLY FOR THE THREE OSRS ITSELF RECOLOURS. Twisted recolours its own model, and",
  "Radiant is a ten-pair recolour of the Oathplate model - which is why its models field says",
  "oathplate. The pairs are RGB15, converted from the cache's HSL16 by the importer's own",
  "hsl16_to_rgb15; a source that matches no face in the model does NOTHING, silently, so battery",
  "group 67 checks every source against the model's real face colours.",
  "",
  "MEMBERSHIP IS THREE PARAMS, NOT A LIST OF NAMES. slayer_headgear is anything that gives the",
  "on-task melee bonus (the masks and every helmet), slayer_helmet is the four protections a helmet",
  "inherits from its parts (helmets only - a bare mask has no earmuffs), and slayer_imbued is the",
  "ranged and magic boost. Adding a colour needs no edit to any proc.",
  "",
  "ONLY TWO CAN BE OBTAINED. red needs an abyssal head and green a Kq head, and those are the two",
  "monsters that exist here. The other twelve have no source and are deliberately kept anyway, so",
  "they can be looked at with ::give; tools/obtainable.py lists them by name rather than being",
  "silenced. black becomes obtainable the moment the King Black Dragon is fightable - a source",
  "block here and nothing else. The rest are post-2013 bosses.",
  "",
  "UNLOCK BITS 5 and 6 in %slayer_unlocks. 0-4 are Gargoyle Smasher, Slug Salter, Reptile",
  "Freezer, Ring Bling and Bigger and Badder."
 ],
